From: Sveinbjorn Geirsson <claude@sveinbjorn.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] fix: retry userptr VM_BIND read-only on EPERM before evicting unused allocations

On the xe KMD a writable userptr bind of a read-only host mapping (a file
mapped r--s, the common case for model weights loaded with mmap) fails with
EPERM from hmm_range_fault. Drm::bindBufferObject treated every bind failure
as memory exhaustion and ran evictUnusedAllocations(), which unbinds the
copy engine command buffer of a still-pending KMD-submitted job (the sweep
only trusts task counts above the engine tag). The blitter then reads the
scratch page, halts on the next mapped allocation, and the next LR-mode
suspend ends in "Engine reset: engine_class=bcs" after the preempt timeout.
Same sweep as GSD-13279 (#973) and GSD-13592 (#1010), different victim.

The GPU only reads such ranges. Retry the bind with the read-only flag
before falling back to the eviction sweep. Measured on Arc A770 / xe 7.3-rc5:
default 16681 EPERM binds and a stall in one llama.cpp run, with the retry
0 failed binds, no staging fallback, prefill +33%, no reset.

Debug key RetryUserptrBindReadOnly=0 restores the previous behaviour.

Signed-off-by: Sveinbjorn Geirsson <claude@sveinbjorn.dev>
---
diff --git a/shared/source/debug_settings/debug_variables_base.inl b/shared/source/debug_settings/debug_variables_base.inl
index 306b51a..cba7140 100644
--- a/shared/source/debug_settings/debug_variables_base.inl
+++ b/shared/source/debug_settings/debug_variables_base.inl
@@ -607,6 +607,7 @@ DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, AddClGlSharing, -1, "Add cl-gl extension")
 DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, EnableBOMmapCreate, -1, "Create BOs using mmap, -1:default, 0:disable(GEM_USERPTR), 1:enable")
 DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, EnableGemCloseWorker, -1, "Use asynchronous gem object closing, -1:default, 0:disable, 1:enable")
 DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, EnableHostPtrValidation, -1, "Validate BO from GEM_USERPTR, -1:default(enable), 0:disable, 1:enable")
+DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, RetryUserptrBindReadOnly, -1, "-1: default (enabled), 0: disabled, 1: enabled. When a writable userptr VM_BIND fails with EPERM (read-only host mapping), retry the bind read-only before evicting unused allocations")
 DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, EnableBlitterOperationsSupport, -1, "-1: default, 0: disable, 1: enable")
 DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, EnableBlitterForEnqueueOperations, -1, "Use Blitter engine for enqueue operations. -1: default, 0: disabled, 1: enabled for every enqueue, 2: disabled, except image from buffer access")
 DECLARE_DEBUG_VARIABLE(int32_t, EnableBlitterForEnqueueImageOperations, -1, "Use Blitter engine for read/write/copy image operations. -1: default, 0: disabled, 1: enabled")
diff --git a/shared/source/os_interface/linux/drm_neo.cpp b/shared/source/os_interface/linux/drm_neo.cpp
index 671a0bb..80d68e3 100644
--- a/shared/source/os_interface/linux/drm_neo.cpp
+++ b/shared/source/os_interface/linux/drm_neo.cpp
@@ -7,6 +7,8 @@
 
 #include "shared/source/os_interface/linux/drm_neo.h"
 
+#include <cerrno>
+
 #include "shared/source/command_stream/command_stream_receiver.h"
 #include "shared/source/command_stream/submission_status.h"
 #include "shared/source/debug_settings/debug_settings_manager.h"
@@ -1842,6 +1844,15 @@ int Drm::bindAddDebugData(OsContext *osContext, BufferObject *bo, uint32_t vmHan
 
 int Drm::bindBufferObject(OsContext *osContext, uint32_t vmHandleId, BufferObject *bo, const bool forcePagingFence) {
     auto ret = changeBufferObjectBinding(this, osContext, vmHandleId, bo, true, forcePagingFence);
+    if (ret != 0 && bo->getUserptr() != 0 && !bo->isReadOnlyGpuResource() && getErrno() == EPERM &&
+        debugManager.flags.RetryUserptrBindReadOnly.get() != 0) {
+        // xe refuses a writable userptr bind of a read-only host range (hmm returns EPERM for
+        // file-backed read-only mappings). The GPU only reads such ranges, so bind read-only
+        // instead of treating EPERM as memory exhaustion: the eviction sweep below unbinds
+        // allocations that other in-flight submissions still use.
+        bo->setAsReadOnly(true);
+        ret = changeBufferObjectBinding(this, osContext, vmHandleId, bo, true, forcePagingFence);
+    }
     if (ret != 0) {
         auto isAsyncFence = bo->isAsyncPagingFenceRequired();
         static_cast<DrmMemoryOperationsHandlerBind *>(this->rootDeviceEnvironment.memoryOperationsInterface.get())->evictUnusedAllocations(false, isAsyncFence);
